Modifications (GPLv3 section 5a)
--------------------------------
This is a modified version of Palmier Pro v0.7.6, changed by Nikhil Dhaliya in 2026:
- Rewritten for Linux in TypeScript on Electron (the original is a Swift/Metal macOS app). The data
  model, editing operations, MCP tool contract, UI texts and translations follow the original.
- Palmier's cloud services (account, credits, hosted generation and transcription) are replaced by
  the user's own API keys (Anthropic, OpenAI, fal, Google, ElevenLabs) and local models
  (whisper.cpp, Silero VAD, Beat This, DeepFilterNet, SigLIP 2, sherpa-onnx speaker models).
- Renamed to Framewright with a new icon. Palmier artwork and trademarks are not used. The
  ".palmier" project package format, the "palmier" export mode and the palmier://models/*
  MCP resources are kept for compatibility with Palmier Pro projects and the MCP contract.

Third-party components
----------------------
Framewright bundles or downloads on first use: Electron, FFmpeg, onnxruntime, sherpa-onnx,
whisper.cpp, lottie-web, React, the Model Context Protocol SDK, and the models listed above. Each is
distributed under its own license. THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt (shipped with the app, generated by
scripts/third-party-licenses.mjs) has the license texts.

FFmpeg: the app bundles the FFmpeg 7.0.2 static build by John Van Sickle (ffmpeg and ffprobe, via
ffmpeg-static b6.1.1), licensed under GPLv3. Its corresponding source, ffmpeg-7.0.2.tar.xz, is attached
to every Framewright release and is also at https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-7.0.2.tar.xz. The
sources of the libraries linked into the build are listed in licenses/FFmpeg-build-sources.txt
(also included in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt).
